#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:2
msgid "📜 Solver logs (:py:mod:`foamlib.logs`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:4
msgid "This module is new and its API may still change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:6
msgid ""
"An OpenFOAM log is written for a disk, not for a reader: a long run produces"
" megabytes of residual lines. :class:`foamlib.logs.FoamLog` reads a log once"
" and answers the questions usually asked of it: did the run finish, did it "
"converge, and if not, why and what to change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:8
msgid ""
"It works on logs from the openfoam.org and openfoam.com distributions, foam-"
"extend and RapidCFD, including logs from utilities such as ``blockMesh``, "
"``snappyHexMesh`` or ``checkMesh``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:11
msgid "Reading a log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:23
msgid ""
":meth:`~foamlib.logs.FoamLog.read` takes a path, "
":meth:`~foamlib.logs.FoamLog.load` an open text or binary file, and "
":meth:`~foamlib.logs.FoamLog.loads` a ``str`` or ``bytes``. All three give "
"the same result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:26
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:28
msgid ""
":meth:`~foamlib.logs.FoamLog.summary` returns a JSON-ready dictionary whose "
"size does not grow with the length of the run (a few kB at most). Lists in "
"it are capped, keeping the most alarming entries first, which makes it "
"suitable for passing to a script, a dashboard or an LLM agent. For a crashed"
" run, part of it looks like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:53
msgid "Per-step data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:55
msgid "Per-step values are kept out of the summary, but remain available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:64
msgid "What the log cannot tell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:66
msgid ""
"Some properties belong to the case rather than to the log, so they are only "
"reported as far as the log shows them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:68
msgid ""
":attr:`~foamlib.logs.FoamLog.steady` is ``None`` unless the log contains "
"evidence either way (SIMPLE or steady-state-mode lines, versus Courant, "
"``deltaT`` or PISO lines). The authoritative answer is ``ddtSchemes`` in "
"``system/fvSchemes``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:69
msgid ""
"Residual trends treat a final residual at or below "
":data:`foamlib.logs.SOLVED_TOL` as solved. Pass ``tolerance=`` (a single "
"value or one per field) with the solver tolerances from "
"``system/fvSolution`` to use the case's own values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:72
msgid "Failure modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../foamlib/docs/logs.rst:74
msgid ""
":data:`foamlib.logs.DIAGNOSTICS` is the table of named failure modes "
"(missing files, boundary condition errors, floating-point exceptions, MPI "
"aborts, meshing failures, ...). Each entry records whether it was confirmed "
"against real logs (:attr:`foamlib.logs.Source.CORPUS`) or only expected from"
" how OpenFOAM behaves and not yet seen in one "
"(:attr:`foamlib.logs.Source.INFERRED`)."
msgstr ""

