#: of foamlib.logs._log.FoamLog.loads:3
msgid ""
"The filename the log was saved under, such as ``\"log.simpleFoam\"``. It is "
"never opened. It is only consulted when the header naming the solver was "
"stripped or blanked, in which case the solver is taken from a "
"``log.<solver>`` filename and :attr:`solver_source` says so. ``None`` skips "
"that fallback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.17/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/foamlib/logs/_log.pydocstring
#: of foamlib.logs._log.FoamLog.loads:8
msgid ""
"The solver tolerance from ``system/fvSolution``, either one value or one per"
" field name. A final residual at or below it counts as solved. Fields not "
"listed use :data:`SOLVED_TOL`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.13.17/x64/lib/python3.13/site-packages/foamlib/logs/_log.pydocstring
#: of foamlib.logs._log.FoamLog.loads:12
msgid ""
":attr:`steady` is ``True`` or ``False`` only when the log says so: a SIMPLE "
"or steady-state-mode line for steady (not from laplacianFoam or "
"scalarTransportFoam, which print SIMPLE lines either way); Courant, "
"``deltaT``, PISO or transient-mode lines for transient. With no evidence, or"
" evidence both ways, it is ``None``: the authoritative answer is "
"``ddtSchemes`` in the case, not the log."
msgstr ""

